\begin_layout Title
China's FAST Telescope: An Overview of Its Structure, Technology, and Scientific
 Achievements
\end_layout

\begin_layout Author
HanYijie 20213006413
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
noindent 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\series bold
Abstract: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
noindent 
\end_layout

\end_inset

The Five-hundred-meter Aperture Spherical Telescope (FAST), also known as
 China’s Sky Eye, is the world's largest single-dish radio telescope.
 Since commencing scientific observations in 2016, FAST has achieved numerous
 breakthroughs in the field of radio astronomy.
 This paper provides a detailed overview of FAST's geographical location,
 unique structural design, advanced focusing technology, and significant
 scientific accomplishments in radio astronomy.
\end_layout

